\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The naPINN framework. The PINN $\hat  u_\theta $ is trained on a PDE loss and a gated data loss. A density estimator with parameters $\phi $ (here an EBM) scores the normalized residuals, a reliability gate maps the standardized log-density to a weight $g_i$ on the data loss, and the rejection cost $\mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {rej}}$ penalizes exclusion.}}{3}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{3}{The naPINN framework. The PINN $\hat u_\theta $ is trained on a PDE loss and a gated data loss. A density estimator with parameters $\phi $ (here an EBM) scores the normalized residuals, a reliability gate maps the standardized log-density to a weight $g_i$ on the data loss, and the rejection cost $\mathcal {L}_{\mathrm {rej}}$ penalizes exclusion}{figure.3}{}}
